 or care yeah so  the  the normal work life here is uh  basically that  we decide uh on on the ideas that we  want to test on our hypothesis  beforehand  and then we try to design experiments so  we asked what predictions  do uh relate to that hypothesis  and then we try to design experiments  that can  specifically test these predictions and  then we look  okay can we use the robot for that or do  we have to observe live  groups or do we have yeah the right  cameras the right software  to investigate the group behavior then  when that is all decided then we go  and ask for the permissions to do the  experiments  and then we start doing the experiments  here in the lab and it's most often it's  a it's a  bout of experimental work then about of  time that you spend  analyzing uh your videos your  observations  your data and then you see okay maybe  that worked out uh pretty well then you  try to  publish that as a result or you go back  to the lab which is most  common procedure and you refine  something and then try it again  so to always have a continuous  improvement of your  experiments that you then can really  answer your questions  this laboratory is part of the  excellence cluster science of  intelligence which is located at the  technical university  the tu and free university and as well  the humboldt university  but we also cooperate with the leibniz  institute for freshwater ecology and  inland fisheries  yeah so the limits with this kind of  experiments  is for sure that we cannot create  a really natural environment for that as  you see here the tank is uh yeah  almost empty so we can't uh allow the  fish to interact with  a lot of structures here because the  robot will yeah  can't uh really swim around them or will  culidate uh  with these structures then so we have to  have a very clean tank  and that is yeah for sure not a  mirroring that what  the animals have in nature so that's why  we always try to complement our research  here in the lab  also 